- The design MUST satisfy EVERY principle of the `karpathy-guidelines` skill document — that document is the SINGLE source (already in your system context and deliberately NOT repeated here), in addition to KISS/DRY.
- Every function, class, module, route, and component must be specified exactly — no "create a service" without specifying the exact interface.
- Include file paths for new files and specify where modifications go in existing files.
- Every `src/**` path cited in design.md MUST either exist on disk TODAY or be declared in task.md (as a created module in a Task action, or as an ephemeral fixture under `## Planned Scaffolds`). The deterministic reconciler (`unrepairable-document-reference`) blocks otherwise — no LLM judgment exempts an undeclared path. Ephemeral test/example fixtures (temp-dir files, throwaway illustrations like `src/a.ts`) MUST be declared under `## Planned Scaffolds`, never cited bare.

